<fn-group>
  <fn id="fn1">
    <label>1</label><p>That is, a calculator providing the energy and
    gradient differences between an atomic structure in an implicit
    solvent and the same structure in vacuum. These differential
    contributions are then added to the energy and gradient components
    of calculations that have no native implementation of solvation
    models (i.e. gas phase-trained MLIPs).</p>
  </fn>
</fn-group>
</back>
</article>
